course: dictionary
lesson: 899
title: Many meanings of bite
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the sentence tells you which one you need. «Bite the apple.» Here bite is a verb: to cut or hold something with your teeth.
explain: Bite can also be a noun, a thing you can name. «A bite to eat» means a small amount of food, and «a dog bite» means the mark a dog leaves with its teeth.
explain: When an insect or snake does it, bite means to hurt with its mouth or sting. «A mosquito bit me.» Ask yourself which meaning fits the words around it.
fact: Bite is a verb and a noun: bite, bites, bit, bitten, biting.
fact: «Bite the apple» means cut or hold something with your teeth.
fact: «A bite to eat» means a small amount of food.
fact: «A dog warns before it bites»: it may yawn, lick its lips, turn its head away, or growl. These are warning signs, so back off.
fact: Never put your fingers near an animal's mouth. Tell an adult about any animal bite.
exercise: In «Bite the apple», what does bite mean? | To hurt with a sting | To wake up suddenly | A small amount of food | *To cut or hold something with your teeth
exercise: «A mosquito bit me.» What does bit mean here? | Ate a small snack | Hid under a bed | Read a book | *Stung or hurt with its mouth
exercise: In «a bite to eat», what is the noun? | A warning sign | *A small amount of food | To cut with teeth | A snake
test: «It bit his hand» is about a rattlesnake. What does bit mean? | *Hurt with its mouth | Read a page | Held a cup | Cooked a meal
test: «A dog warns before it bites.» Which of these is a warning sign? | *Turns its head away | Eats its dinner | Climbs a tree | Sings a song
exam: «The startled hamster bit his finger hard.» What does bit mean here? | *Hurt with its teeth | Jumped on a bed | Hid under a blanket | Ate a whole meal
